Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-100: twenty on the stage, not six - a new $500
 account

Owner directive 2026-09-21 (David): "I don't care if I lose that $500
just start with a new $500. It's fake anyway... The answer is we don't
need six. I don't care if it's written into the policy - we get to
decide exactly what we're building."

The funnel already started at ~600 (612 USD pairs swept, ~500 coins
collected a minute, ~90 ranked, 20 offered, 20 order books carried by
the tape after FIX-99). It then hit a wall of SIX:
policy.universe.preparationSlots = 6 prepared six of the twenty, and
execution/feed.js admitted six CANDIDATEs inside a twelve-symbol hot
set (CANDIDATE_SLOTS_FULL / HOT_SET_FULL - the shape behind the live
FEED_NOT_IN_TAPE_UNIVERSE refusals). composition.js prepares
Math.min(preparationSlots, maxCandidates), so both had to move.

  maxCandidates     6 -> 20
  maxHotSet        12 -> 40
  preparationSlots  6 -> 20

A policy binding is immutable per account (ACCOUNT_POLICY_MISMATCH on
any byte), so this IS a new account: paper-starting-styles-usd500-
fee080-wide20, same $500, same 0.80% taker, same limits, same 10s
proposal law, same six setups, same PAPER authority. The old account
and its journal are untouched on disk - left behind, never reset.

Frozen core UNCHANGED (judge/*.js, execution/*.js, watch/watch.js);
judge/samples/policy.paper-reference.json stays at 6/12/6 so the
divergence is this account's, not silent global drift.

Fenced by test/publish-fix-100-twenty-on-the-stage.test.js (6) and the
widened-universe carve-out in test/paper-e2e-pg.test.js. Recorded as
docs/JUDGE-PAPER-AUDIT.md 4.37.

